/-
  GPn10T.lean — generalized Petersen graphs GP(n,10), n ≥ 21: the colouring (tables and definitions).

  GP(n,10) = `GPk.gp n 10` (see GPPeriodic.lean): u_i = 2i, v_i = 2i+1; edges 3i: u_i u_{i+1}, 3i+1: u_i v_i,
  3i+2: v_i v_{i+10}.  Colouring: for n ≥ 39 a periodic part of period 6 (patterns P0..P5; block
  J < n - n mod 6 - 12 gets P_(J mod 6)) followed by a seam of length n mod 6 + 12 that depends on n mod 6;
  explicit colourings for 21 ≤ n < 39.  A pattern is [outer, spoke, inner] with colours 0..4.
  The tables were found by a SAT search on 2026-10-02 (search/gpsearch.py, search/gp10.json); this file was generated
  by search/gen_gpk.py.  The Lean proof does not depend on the search: all windows are checked by `decide`.
-/
